content.text:
Now game.js — big. Split maybe into two files? It's the core. Could put entities/AI in enemies.js and game loop in game.js, but more integration hassle. Let me write game.js in one go, maybe 700 lines. To avoid output limit, write in two parts: first game.js core (state, input, loop, UI, start/round), then append with edit? Writing whole content ~ maybe 20k tokens; risky for limit. Break into two writes: game.js with imports/state/UI/input/start, and js/combat.js with enemies AI + shooting + rounds? Better modular:

- js/game.js: bootstrap, state, input, update loop, UI, rounds, render.
- js/combat.js: weapon config, shooting logic, damage, enemy AI/update, spawn, particles.

Circular deps? combat needs game state and callbacks. Export functions taking game/context. Let's design combat.js exports:
```
export const WEAPONS
export function createWeapons()
export function spawnEnemies(world, player, count, rand)
export function updateEnemies(game, dt, hooks)
export function shoot(game, world, audio, hooks)
export function enemyShoot...
```
Hooks maybe circular. Simpler: combat.js exports classes/functions that accept a `game` object with methods `damagePlayer`, `onKill`, `spawnParticles`, `alert`, etc. game.js defines those.

Let's implement combat.js:

```js
import { WEAPONS? } ...
export const WEAPONS = {...};
export const WEAPON_ORDER = ['ak','usp','knife'];
export function makeLoadout(){...}
export function enemyFromSpawn(x,y,variant,i,frames)
export function attemptShoot(game, world, audio)
export function reloadWeapon(game, audio)
export function switchWeapon(game, id, audio)
export function updateEnemies(game, world, dt, audio)
export function spawnEnemies(world, player, count, frames)
```

game object shape:
```
game.player {x,y,angle,pitch,health,armor,weapon,weapons:{ak:{ammo,reserve},usp:...},cooldown,reloading,reloadTotal,recoil,flash,swing,bob,sway,moving,crouch}
game.enemies
game.particles
game.shots, hits, kills, headshots, money
game.roundActive
game.state
game.shake, hurt, muzzle, hitmarker, hitmarkerHead
game.weaponAnim...
game.world? 
game.hud? 
```
Functions:
- `requestPointerLock` not needed.
- `game.addKillFeed(text)` maybe UI in game.js; combat calls game.onKill(e, headshot).

Implement callbacks:
```
game.damagePlayer(amount, source)
game.onKill(enemy, headshot, weaponName)
game.spawnBlood(x,y,z)
game.spawnDust(x,y,z,nx,ny)
```
Simplify combat.js handles particles directly by pushing into game.particles.

Shoot:
```
export function tryShoot(game, world, audio){
 const p=game.player; const w=WEAPONS[p.weapon];
 if(p.reloading>0 || p.cooldown>0) return;
 if(p.weapon==='knife'){ ...; return; }
 const st=p.weapons[p.weapon];
 if(st.ammo<=0){ audio.empty(); p.cooldown=0.25; game.startReload?.(); return; }
 st.ammo--; game.shots++;
 p.cooldown=w.rate; p.recoil=Math.min(1, p.recoil+0.34); p.flash=1; game.muzzle=0.07; game.shake=Math.max(game.shake, 2.4);
 p.pitch += w.kick + Math.random()*1.5;
 p.angle += (Math.random()-0.5)*w.rate*0.6;
 audio.shoot(w.sound);
 const spread=...
 const angle = p.angle + (Math.random()+Math.random()-1)*spread;
 const dx=Math.cos(angle), dy=Math.sin(angle);
 const wall=world.raycast(p.x,p.y,dx,dy,w.range);
 let maxT = wall? wall.dist : w.range;
 let best=null, bestHead=false;
 for (const e of game.enemies){ if(!e.alive) continue; ... }
 if(best){ ... damage; hits++; ... } else if(wall){ dust particles }
 if(st.ammo===0) { p.autoReload = 0.25? } // trigger reload automatically after delay maybe
}
```
Spread: w.spread (radians) * (p.moving?2.2:1) * (p.crouch?0.7:1) * (1 + p.recoil*0.3). Use random centered: `(Math.random()-0.5)*2*spread` plus recoil.

Aim vertical: `const aimY = 0.5 + (p.pitch * t) / game.renderH;` but pitch recoil bumps; game.renderH from renderer.H. Use game.viewH updated each frame.

Hitbox: if aimY > 0.60 → head radius 0.20; else body radius 0.30, and aimY > 0.02. If aimY > 1.05 (above head) no hit. Also if aimY < 0.05 (floor) no hit.

Select nearest t; if head hit, damage w.head; else w.damage. Headshot should kill always when head>=100. Add damage falloff? AK body 34, 3 hits. Good.

On enemy hit: blood particles at (e.x,e.y, 0.55), e.hitFlash=0.12, e.health-=dmg, e.alerted=true, audio.hit(head). If health<=0: e.alive=false; e.deadTimer=0; game.kills++; game.money+=300; if head game.headshots++; audio.kill(); game.onKill?.(e, head); push blood more; if all dead and roundActive → game.roundWon(); (call callback game.checkRound?). Expose `game.onEnemyKilled(e, head)`.

Knife:
```
if cooldown<=0: cooldown=0.42; p.swing=1; audio.knife();
 find enemy within 2.2 and angle diff<1.0 and LOS → damage 58; head false.
```
Also knife has no ammo.

Reload:
```
export function startReload(game,audio){
 const p=game.player, w=WEAPONS[p.weapon];
 if(p.weapon==='knife'||p.reloading>0) return;
 const st=p.weapons[p.weapon];
 if(st.ammo>=w.mag||st.reserve<=0) return;
 p.reloading=w.reload; p.reloadTotal=w.reload; audio.reload(w.reload);
}
```
Update in game.js: decrement reloading; when <=0 transfer:
Can implement in combat `updateWeapon(game,dt,audio)`:
```
p.cooldown=max(0,p.cooldown-dt); p.recoil=max(0,p.recoil-dt*2.6); p.flash=max(0,p.flash-dt*8); p.swing=max(0,p.swing-dt*3);
if(p.reloading>0){p.reloading-=dt; if(p.reloading<=0){...transfer...; p.reloading=0;}}
```
Sound handled at start.

Switch weapon: if knife no ammo; p.weapon=id; p.reloading=0; p.cooldown=Math.max(p.cooldown,0.25); audio.click.

Enemy AI update. Need world.findPath; frames (texture sets) passed in spawnEnemies from renderer.tex.enemies? Renderer holds textures; game can access renderer.tex.enemies. Pass `frameSets` to spawnEnemies.

Enemy fields:
```
{ id, x,y,angle, health, alive, variant, frames: set, alerted:false, cooldown:1+rand, fireTimer:0, walkPhase:rand*6, moving:false, path:[], pathTimer:0, hitFlash:0, deadTimer:0, strafe:1, strafeTimer:1+rand*2, name:`T-0${i+1}` }
```

Update:
```
for e:
 if(!alive){ e.deadTimer+=dt; e.fireTimer=0; continue; }
 e.hitFlash-=dt; e.fireTimer-=dt; e.cooldown-=dt; e.strafeTimer-=dt;
 const dx=player.x-e.x, dy=... dist
 const angTo=atan2(dy,dx)
 const los = dist<24 && world.lineOfSight(e.x,e.y,player.x,player.y);
 if(los && dist<18) e.alerted=true;
 if(!e.alerted){
   // idle scan slowly; occasionally reposition? keep still to avoid wandering into weird spots.
   e.moving=false;
   e.angle += Math.sin(game.time*0.5+e.id)*dt*0.2;
   continue;
 }
 // face
 e.angle = angleLerp(e.angle, angTo, 1-Math.exp(-dt*7))
 e.moving=false;
 const moveSpeed = 2.15;
 let mx=0,my=0;
 if(los){
   if(dist>6.5){ mx=dx/dist; my=dy/dist; }
   else if(dist<2.6){ mx=-dx/dist; my=-dy/dist; }
   else {
     // strafe
     const side = e.strafe;
     mx = -dy/dist*side; my = dx/dist*side;
     if(e.strafeTimer<=0){ e.strafe*=-1; e.strafeTimer=1.1+Math.random()*1.8; }
   }
   // shooting
   if(dist<17 && e.cooldown<=0 && game.roundActive){
     e.cooldown=0.8+Math.random()*0.85;
     e.fireTimer=0.13;
     const pan = Math.sin(angTo-player.angle); // approximate
     audio.enemyShot(pan, dist);
     const pMoving = player.moving?1:0;
     const chance = Math.max(0.14, Math.min(0.78, 0.86 - dist*0.035 - pMoving*0.12 - (player.crouch?0.08:0)));
     if(Math.random()<chance){
        const dmg = 9+Math.random()*9;
